      "prompt": "Rationalise the denominator of \\frac{10}{9 - √14}, giving your answer in its simplest form.",
      "solution_steps": [
        "Multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate of the denominator, (9 + √14):",
        "\\frac{10}{9 - √14}",
        "= \\frac{10(9 + √14)}{[(9 - √14)(9 + √14)]}",
        "The denominator is a difference of two squares: 9^2 - 14 = 67",
        "The numerator is 10(9 + √14) = 90 + 10√14",
        "= \\frac{90 + 10√14}{67}"
